{"name":"Bogart","hex":"#8b8274","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Bogart","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["An English surname from Dutch, most famously borne by American actor Humphrey Bogart."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To behave in a manner similar to the on-screen characters portrayed by Humphrey Bogart."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Bogart"}],"entries":[{"title":"Humphrey Bogart","blocks":[{"text":"Humphrey DeForest Bogart, nicknamed Bogie, was an American actor. Often known for his leading roles as both gangsters and detectives in film noirs, his performances in classic Hollywood cinema made him an American cultural icon. He won an Academy Award and was honored with a star on the Hollywood Walk of Fame in 1960."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Humphrey_Bogart_by_Elmer_Fryer_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Humphrey_Bogart_by_Elmer_Fryer_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Humphrey_Bogart"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/245_W103_St_Bogie_plaque_jeh.JPG/500px-245_W103_St_Bogie_plaque_jeh.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/245_W103_St_Bogie_plaque_jeh.JPG/1280px-245_W103_St_Bogie_plaque_jeh.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/245_W103_St_Bogie_plaque_jeh.JPG/500px-245_W103_St_Bogie_plaque_jeh.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Plaque commemorating Bogart's birthplace, 245 W. 103rd St., New York City","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A245_W103_St_Bogie_plaque_jeh.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Maud_Humphrey_from_American_Women%2C_1897_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Maud_Humphrey_from_American_Women%2C_1897_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Maud_Humphrey_from_American_Women%2C_1897_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Maud_Humphrey_from_American_Women%2C_1897_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Maud Humphrey in the 1897 book American Women","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMaud_Humphrey_from_American_Women%2C_1897_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Humphrey_Bogart_yearbook_photo_-_1918.jpg/500px-Humphrey_Bogart_yearbook_photo_-_1918.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Humphrey_Bogart_yearbook_photo_-_1918.jpg/500px-Humphrey_Bogart_yearbook_photo_-_1918.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Enlisting at 18 in the U.S. Navy in 1918, Bogart was recorded as a model sailor.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHumphrey_Bogart_yearbook_photo_-_1918.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Swifty_Humphrey_Bogart_1922_newspaper.png/500px-Swifty_Humphrey_Bogart_1922_newspaper.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Swifty_Humphrey_Bogart_1922_newspaper.png/1280px-Swifty_Humphrey_Bogart_1922_newspaper.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Swifty_Humphrey_Bogart_1922_newspaper.png/500px-Swifty_Humphrey_Bogart_1922_newspaper.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bogart was praised in an October 15, 1922, newspaper review of the play Swifty: \"Humphrey Bogart as t